What is the purpose of the change
Scan data using a specified tag or branch.
Brief change log
Add the following syntax
SQL:
* SELECT * FROM sample /*+ OPTIONS('tag'='t1')*/ ;
* SELECT * FROM sample /*+ OPTIONS('branch'='t1')*/ ;
API:
    public Builder tag(String tag) {
      contextBuilder.useTag(tag);
      return this;
    }

    public Builder branch(String branch) {
      contextBuilder.useBranch(branch);
      return this;
    }
    public Builder startTag(String startTag) {
      contextBuilder.startTag(startTag);
      return this;
    }

    public Builder endTag(String endTag) {
      contextBuilder.endTag(endTag);
      return this;
    }

This replaces a bunch of code of the form
try {
      // do something
      Assert.fail(...);
    } catch (Exception e) {
        // make sure exception has correct message/code/...
    }

There are still a few legit places left that use Assert.fail() so I didn't create a checkstyle rule to prevent usage

